   "tag": "aside"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-11-16, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " code and sheet, 2026-10-17. Linear ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-27"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " (dossier / transparent view), with ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-24"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " (registry placeholder ARNs). Synthetic tests only in git."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The ledger is the machine-readable list of what was absent from a source or withheld from view, and why. It feeds a fully transparent HeavyMap view mode: empty, stale, placeholder, contradictory, too-sparse or corrupted, screened, and out-of-coverage are named, not painted over. Overlay slivers are a display rule (",
    {
     "children": [
      "flag, never extinguish"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", PI-0063), not a gap type."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "This is plumbing under the four-concept frame. It is not a fifth product name. Absence on a ladder rung is still a Claim & Refusal refusal reason. Gap types below are a finer honesty vocabulary for held data and for screened fields. They do not add a fourth refusal reason."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Inventory: ",
    {
     "children": [
      "Spreadsheets/20-data-gaps-ledger.csv"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (source of truth). Loader: ",
    {
     "children": [
      "industrial_atlas/gaps.py"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Per-parcel ids travel on the dossier record; repeated text stays in the ledger and the dossier manifest."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
